<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A ceiling on any single test, so a hang is a named failure instead of a silent leg.

  Every test here talks to a daemon, and several connect over descriptors that are not daemon
  sockets on purpose. Whether such a connect completes, is refused, or waits forever for a handshake
  depends on the PipeWire version underneath, which differs between a developer machine and a CI
  runner. An await with no deadline turns the last of those into a run that produces no output at
  all: the step sits until the job's own limit kills it, and the log ends at the command echo with
  nothing to say which test was running.

  The number is deliberately far above any real test. The slowest legitimate tests here are the
  daemon end-to-end ones at roughly a minute, so five minutes cannot fire on a test that is merely
  slow - it only catches one that is never coming back.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <MSTest>
    <TestTimeout>300000</TestTimeout>
  </MSTest>
</RunSettings>
